course: dictionary
lesson: 1731
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. «The ancient Egyptian civilization» means a large, organised society with cities, government, laws and writing.
explain: «The history of civilization» means human society in general and everything people have achieved. Look at the clues around the word. Cities and rulers point to the first meaning, while all of human society over time points to the second.
explain: The third meaning is informal and a little funny. «After camping we were glad to be back in civilization.» Here it means comfortable modern life with shops, toilets and internet. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Civilization means a large, organised society with cities, government, laws, writing, art and trade.
fact: Early civilizations include Sumer, Egypt, the Indus Valley, China, Greece, Rome, the Maya, the Aztecs and the Benin Kingdom.
fact: «Civilization» can also mean human society in general, especially its achievements: «the history of civilization».
fact: Informally, «civilization» can mean comfortable modern life with shops and internet, as in «back in civilization».
fact: In the past, some people called other peoples «uncivilized» to excuse unfair treatment, so use this word carefully.
exercise: «The ancient Egyptian civilization built great cities.» What does civilization mean here? | A group of friends who play games | *A large, organised society with cities and laws | A kind of weather | Shops, toilets and internet
exercise: «After camping we were glad to be back in civilization.» What does civilization mean in this sentence? | The ancient past | A type of camping tent | A battle between two armies | *Comfortable modern life with shops, toilets and internet
exercise: In «the history of civilization», what does civilization mean? | A small village with one shop | A video game about building cities | A type of weather | *Human society in general and its achievements
test: Sam says civilization is just the name of a game. What is the right answer? | *No, the game is called Civilization, but the word itself means a large, organised society | Yes, it means camping with no toilets | Yes, the word only ever means a game | No, it means only a small village
test: Which of these is an early civilization? | *The Maya | Comfortable modern life | A type of weather | Camping in the woods
exam: Why should you check the context before deciding what civilization means? | Because civilization always means a game | *Because the word has more than one meaning, and the sentence shows which one, so you can ignore the rest of the text | Because the word is never used in history | Because the word has more than one meaning, and the sentence shows which one
